 the  Ripper  but Carpenter hasn't shied away from  performing in front of the camera as  well since leaving Dexter behind the  actress has sought out similar success  on the small screen that search  ultimately led the actress to the  hyper-competitive realm of network  television where she's delivered strong  work in largely forgettable dramas the  first of carpenters post Dexter TV roles  came on the short-lived dramedy  limitless which was based on the Bradley  Cooper starring movie of the same name  that flick found Cooper  the life fantastic after ingesting a  wonder drug that enabled him to utilize  the full potential of his brain the  television adaptation which was produced  by Cooper and Joker director Todd  Phillips followed a similar set up this  time however the gifted man is out to  make the world a safer place and  Carpenter portrays the FBI agent tasked  with helping focus the man's energies on  solving crimes you will have plenty of  stuff to go through the morning  carpenters next television venture found  her playing the other side of the law as  a traitorous former CIA agent forced to  team up with the FBI  to help track down their most-wanted spy  titled the enemy within  carpenters timely espionage drama had  the look of a winner when it hit the air  in 2019 but tragically never found its  audience and was cancelled after airing  just 13 episodes  the actress seems to have had better  luck on the big screen having found a  patron of sorts in cinematic rabble  rouser s Kraig Kahler  whose modern b-movie marvels include  brawl in cell block 99 and 2019 s  disturbing dirty cop caper dragged  across concrete in the hyper violent  brawl in cell block 99 carpenter plays  alar and Thomas the wife of Vince  Vaughn's Bradley Thomas a retired boxer  whose life of crime lands him behind  bars at the Redleaf Correctional  Facility where his troubles only grow  more intense throughout it all Carpenter  stayed devoted to the madness while  breathing necessar